      "text": "First, I need to find the prime factorization of both 40 and 48.\n\n40 can be written as: 2 x 2 x 2 x 5 = 2^3 x 5\n48 can be written as: 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 = 2^4 x 3\n\nTo find the GCF, I need to take the product of the lowest powers of the common prime factors. In this case, the two prime factors shared by both numbers are 2 and 3. The lowest power of 2 in both numbers is 2^3, and the lowest power of 3 is 3^0. \n\nSo, multiplying these values gives me the GCF: 2^3 x 3^0 = 8.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common factor of 40 and 48 is 8.",
